body:
Craft revise after relay — pick ONE for this pass: --list-rules (C1 = P1 = E1).

@product: supporting P1 as the consensus candidate. Discoverability without heuristic sprawl matches craft's architecture goal: export rule metadata from src/rules.ts so cli/glossary cannot drift. P2 (siblings table) is useful docs but orthogonal; park it. P3 stays good signal but is content, not structure.

@experience: supporting E1; E2 (print rule id in report) is a natural follow-on once the catalog is exported — do not bundle into this pass or we grow scope. Counter soft on E3/--exclude for this round: more parse/filter surface than a list-rules early exit.

@reliability: counter R1 as the *single* ship this pass. Conflict-markers (R1/C3/P3) is high-confidence and I still want it next — but architecturally we keep adding rules while rules() stays closed and help/glossary can lie. R2/--exclude improves grade honesty; also larger than list-rules. Prefer R1 as the next pass after catalog exists so the new rule id is listable on day one.

Craft single preference: --list-rules only. Park C2 severity-unify and C3 conflict-markers.

Experience pick for this pass: ONE idea = --list-rules (E1 ≡ P1 ≡ C1).

@craft: support C1 — exporting a catalog from rules.ts then printing it from cli.ts is the right UX SSOT; glossary already says ids may evolve, so the CLI must be the discoverable source. Park C2 (severity unify) as a follow-up — valuable craft, but invisible to users this pass.

@product: support P1 over P2/P3 for the single ship. Sibling docs (P2) are useful later; they do not fix the gap that CI/humans cannot list heuristic identity without opening source.

@reliability: counter R1 (and soft-counter @craft C3 / @product P3) as the ONE idea this round. Conflict-markers is high-precision and I would ship it next — but it adds another opaque finding title without a catalog, which worsens discoverability. Also park R2/E3 --exclude and R3 debug-leftovers; noise filters are UX-relevant but larger surface than a catalog flag.

Experience preference: ship --list-rules only. Optional tiny companion if consensus allows a one-liner: print rule id in formatText (E2) — otherwise defer E2 too.
